{
  "id": 426367669,
  "iid": 22036,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Take application flavor out of capture functionality",
  "description": "The capture functionality was designed for packet capture interfaces, that not all \"applications\" have (i.e. Stratoshark).  The changes here:\n\n1. Separate the functions that get interfaces between Wireshark and Stratoshark (get_interface_list_ws and get_interface_list_ss, respectively).  This way dumpcap can call the function needed based on its application flavor.\n2. get_remote_interface_list() now has a parameter to determine if client wants \"network interfaces\" (i.e. Wireshark) so higher layers can determine the application flavor\n3. Have dumpcap implement a \"local\" application flavor. It should be the only application that really needs to support all capturing applications at the same time.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2025-10-24T18:38:01.372Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-10-29T14:14:38.298Z",
