      ],
      "title": "Take application flavor out of capture functionality",
      "message": "Take application flavor out of capture functionality\n\nThe capture functionality was designed for packet capture interfaces, that not all \"applications\" have (i.e. Stratoshark).  The changes here:\n\n1. Separate the functions that get interfaces between Wireshark and Stratoshark (get_interface_list_ws and get_interface_list_ss, respectively).  This way dumpcap can call the function needed based on its application flavor.\n2. get_remote_interface_list() now has a parameter to determine if client wants \"network interfaces\" (i.e. Wireshark) so higher layers can determine the application flavor\n3. Have dumpcap implement a \"local\" application flavor. It should be the only application that really needs to support all capturing applications at the same time.\n",
      "author_name": "Michael Mann",
      "author_email": "mmann78@netscape.net",
      "authored_date": "2025-10-24T09:26:40.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "Michael Mann",
